 all time.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/53"} "Dorothy Holman"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/59"} "Kitty McKane"] " of Britain were also top players.  The strongest international players missing were " [:a {:href "/athletes/1029"} "Molla Mallory"] " (né Bjurstedt) of the United States, a Norwegian emigré who had won a bronze medal in ladies’ singles at the " [:a {:href "/results/44501"} "1912 Olympics in Stockholm"] "; " [:a {:href "/athletes/57"} "Dorothea Lambert Chambers"] " of Great Britain, a four-time Wimbledon singles champion who had won the " [:a {:href "/results/44309"} "Olympic singles gold medal in 1908"] "; and Elizabeth Ryan of the United States, who would be runner-up in 1921 at Wimbledon to Miss Lenglen, but who was best known as a doubles player.  It is unlikely they would have challenged Miss Lenglen.  Lenglen won the gold medal without losing a set, and gave up only four games.  In her first three matches, she won both sets at love, lost one game to " [:a {:href "/athletes/2594"} "Sigrid Fick"] " in the semi-finals, and three to Dorothy Holman in the finals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2455"} "Suzanne Lenglen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/53"} "Dorothy Holman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59"} "Kitty Mc